  "problem": "${\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{2}^{i+j}=$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we write out the inner summation by summing over the index $i:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{2}^{i+j} & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}[{\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{2}^{i+j}] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}({2}^{1+j}+{2}^{2+j}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}({2}^{1+j}+{2}^{2+j})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we sum over the index $j:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}({2}^{1+j}+{2}^{2+j}) & =({2}^{1+1}+{2}^{2+1})+({2}^{2+1}+{2}^{2+2}) \\\\  & =(4+8)+(8+16) \\\\  & =36\\end{aligned}\n$$",
